  "body": "There is no way to specify lossless compression for the webp codec. Chrome seems to treat a quality of 1 as lossless (which is not really correct). There were discussions about adding a third parameter specifying a lossless flag or adding a special mimetype for losslesswebp. However, the only logical thing in my opinion is to allow to pass an object as second parameter with the encoderOptions (funny enough MDN already calls the second parameter \"encoderOptions\" which would suggest an object).\r\n\r\nThis solution would allow for more specific encoder options as well. webp alone has tons of it. Options that are not supported by the browser could simply be ignored.\r\n",
